Pe dată de 2011-07-07 10:53, Stephen a scris:
> Hello there.  I an currently on the first level on the dungeon, and
> have encountered 3 locked doors.  No matter where I look, I can't seem
> to find a key.
> my question is: if I encounter a dungeon level with locked doors, is
> there a guarantee that the key can always be found on the same level?
> I think I've discovered all the secret passageways on this level, and
> I don't like kicking down doors unnecessarily.
> Hope you can help.
> Thanks
Having to kick down some doors at the beginning is rather normal for
most roles, AFAIK.  The only relationship between closed-off spaces and
items I know is that a scroll of teleportation is always generated in a
completely isolated cabinet (i.e. a single free space immediately
outside the wall of a room, with no door or corridors leading to it).
Otherwise, you might get stuck there with no way to continue the game,
e.g. if you identify your first scroll of teleportation by reading it
and consequently find yourself there.

Before kicking, explore as much as possible of the level, listen for the
environment sounds which might indicate special rooms, and especially
make sure there isn't and never was the inscription “closed for
inventory” on the floor in front of the door you want to kick down.


